A1. Moth fodder. ~ CLOTHES
A7. Stupid, numb, thick, simple, dumb, or how are you? ~ ASININE
A13. A little pig. ~ RUNT
A14. When bachelors chase pretty girls this is what the girls usually do to them. ~ CATCH
A16. Halitosis is this kind of turpitude. ~ ORAL
A17. This is unrefined. ~ ORE
A18. The life of the party. ~ ALCOHOL
A20. The first loudspeaker. ~ EVE
A21. You and I. ~ WE
A22. What seven days without food makes one. ~ WEAK
A23. The land of shillalahs and begorras. ~ ERIN
A25. Yataghan Carriers (init.). ~ YC
A26. The reason for the absence of white collar jobs in Pittsburgh. ~ SOOT
A28. A party, spree, or bender. ~ TEAR
A30. To be on fire. (Hot stuff!) ~ BURN
A31. The uninvited guest—at picnics. ~ ANT
A33. Something fat people have a hard time staying on. ~ DIET
A35. This is found in flasks of lightning. ~ KICK
A36. The starting place of many marvelous fights. ~ ALTAR
A38. Meager. ~ LEAN
A40. Advice to bachelors—don't say it with this. ~ INK
A41. This knocks me cold. ~ ASPIRIN
A43. Falsehood. ~ LIE
A44. A sky pilot (abbr.). ~ DD
A45. These animals have large prominent teeth. ~ ELKS
A46. Sock breakers. ~ TOES
A48. An island near New York City (abbr.). ~ LI
A49. These go with the crafts. ~ ARTS
A51. Tight. (Nothing to do with tippling.) ~ TAUT
A53. This means "hear" in Latin. ~ AUDIO
A55. The cry of a sinking schooner. ~ SOS
A57. Something pretty school-teachers do. ~ TEACH
A59. Scheme. ~ PLAN
A60. Things that prize fighters playfully place on their opponent's proboscis. ~ SOCKS
A62. A thin flat piece of anything. ~ SLAB
A63. Pennsylvania Tomato Munchers (init.). ~ PTM
A64. The part of a joy ride that flappers dislike. ~ WALKING
A66. Crazy Newfoundland Ostriches (init.). ~ CNO
A67. Interjection of amateur orators. ~ ER
A68. Export product of Italy. ~ DAGO
A69. Ancient boat builder. ~ NOAH
A71. A fellow whose mistakes are buried (abbr.) ~ DR
A72. Ethiopian persuaders. (Ask the man who hones one!) ~ RAZORS
A73. Lover's lanes. ~ BYWAYS

D1. Something a king always has on his mind. ~ CROWN
D2. Entice. ~ LURE
D3. A lonesome number. ~ ONE
D4. Tom Thumb's initials. ~ TT
D5. A burst of applause. ~ ECLAT
D6. To fire with enthusiasm. ~ SACK
D7. A pain in the neck. ~ ACHE
D8. Without sheckles. ~ SHORT
D9. Feminine affirmative. ~ NO
D10. Crossword anger. ~ IRE
D11. Join this, and see the next world. ~ NAVY
D12. Choose by preference. ~ ELECT
D15. Preposition. ~ TO
D18. A long time. ~ AEON
D19. Toyed with the truth. ~ LIED
D22. Labor. ~ WORK
D24. Something most people have right at their finger tips. ~ NAIL
D26. One way to get rid of a sucker. ~ SUCK
D27. Against. ~ ANTI
D29. Bootleg progression. ~ REEL
D30. What many matrimonial ties do. ~ BIND
D31. Yodeling hills. ~ ALPS
D32. Made by the Queen of Hearts. ~ TART
D34. The end of a good old horse. ~ TAIL
D35. A fellow who grabs 'em young. ~ KIDNAPPER
D36. What a wife does when she wants to know why her husband didn't get home until three in the morning. ~ ASKS
D37. Fun in Herrin. ~ RIOT
D39. Professional borrowers. ~ NEIGHBORS
D41. High. ~ ALTO
D42. But not gawdy! ~ NEAT
D45. The land of more shillalahs and begorras. ~ ERIN
D47. What a chorus girl does to your old man. ~ SUES
D49. A famous race starter. ~ ADAM
D50. An east side diamond. ~ ROCK
D52. Something face powder is made from. ~ TALC
D54. Very much so and then some. ~ ULTRA
D55. A tenor's lament. ~ SOLO
D56. A kind of a game that's played in Florida. ~ SKIN
D58. This is sweet stuff. ~ CANDY
D60. Sinks down. ~ SAGS
D61. A high hatter. ~ SNOB
D64. Sherman's synonym for Satan's Sanctum Sanctorum. ~ WAR
D65. Full of spirits (hic!). ~ GAY
D68. Something doers do. ~ DO
D70. Heavy wives (init.). ~ HW


